{"strongs": "H3576", "word": "כָּזַב", "translit": "ka.zav", "root": "כור", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "lie, be a liar", "definition": "[ כָּזַב ] verb lie, be a liar (Arabic ; Aramaic כְּדַב , id. chiefly Pa`el; Late Hebrew כָּזַב ) — Qal Participle כָּלהָֿאָדָם כֹּזֵב Ps 116:11 (compare כָּזָּב Ps 62:10 ). Niph`al Perfect 3 feminine singular תֹּחַלְתּוֺ נִכְזָ֑בָה Job 41:1 his hope has been made deceptive , i.e. been shewn to be so; 2 masculine singular consecutive וְנִכְזָ֑בְתָּ Prov 30:6 lest he convict thee and thou be proven a liar. Pi`el Perfect 3 masculine singular כִּזֵּב Mic 2:11 Imperfect 3 masculine singular יְכַזֵּב Hab 2:3 ; Prov 14:5 וִיכַזֵּב Num 23:19 , etc.; Infinitive construct suffix כַזֶּבְכֶם ( בְּ ) Ezek 13:19 — 1. lie, tell a lie , absolute, Num 23:19 ( J E ), Mic 2:11 ; Job 6:28 ; Job 34:6 ; Prov 14:5 ; Isa 57:11 followed by לְ person lie to Ezek 13:9 ; Ps 78:36 ; Ps 89:36 followed by בְּ person tell a lie with , i.e. in intercourse, conversation with 2Kgs 4:16 . 2. disappoint, fail , of a divine revelation Hab 2:3 waters of a spring Isa 58:11 . Hiph`il Imperfect 3 masculine singular suffix יַכְזִיבֵנִי Job 24:25 who will make me a liar ? i.e. prove me to be so (compare Niph`al )", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3975')\">BDB3975</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3576')\">H3576</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3974')\">BDB3974</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3976')\">BDB3976</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>כָּזַב</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>lie, be a liar</highlightword> (Arabic <placeholder2487/>; Aramaic <bdbarc>כְּדַב</bdbarc>, <placeholder2488/> <highlight>id.</highlight> chiefly Pa`el; Late Hebrew <bdbheb>כָּזַב</bdbheb>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Participle</highlight> <bdbheb>כָּלהָֿאָדָם כֹּזֵב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 116:11\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"116\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"116\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(19,116,11)\">Ps 116:11</ref> (compare <bdbheb>כָּזָּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 62:10\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"62\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"62\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(19,62,10)\">Ps 62:10</ref>). <b>Niph`al</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 3 feminine singular <bdbheb>תֹּחַלְתּוֺ נִכְזָ֑בָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 41:1\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(18,41,1)\">Job 41:1</ref> <highlight>his hope has been made deceptive</highlight>, i.e. been shewn to be so; 2 masculine singular consecutive <bdbheb>וְנִכְזָ֑בְתָּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 30:6\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(20,30,6)\">Prov 30:6</ref> lest he convict thee <highlight>and thou be proven a liar.</highlight> <b>Pi`el</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 3 masculine singular <bdbheb>כִּזֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Mic 2:11\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(33,2,11)\">Mic 2:11</ref> <highlight>Imperfect</highlight> 3 masculine singular <bdbheb>יְכַזֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hab 2:3\" b=\"35\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(35,2,3)\">Hab 2:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 14:5\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(20,14,5)\">Prov 14:5</ref> <bdbheb>וִיכַזֵּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Num 23:19\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(4,23,19)\">Num 23:19</ref>, etc.; <highlight>Infinitive construct</highlight> suffix <bdbheb>כַזֶּבְכֶם</bdbheb> (<bdbheb>בְּ</bdbheb>) <ref ref=\"Ezek 13:19\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(26,13,19)\">Ezek 13:19</ref> — </div><div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>lie, tell a lie</highlight>, absolute, <ref ref=\"Num 23:19\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(4,23,19)\">Num 23:19</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup><lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('E')\"><reflink>E</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"